{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "reconstructed_statement": "Let E be any complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with a normed additive commutative group structure and its Borel measurable structure, and let S be any measurable space. Zero-dimensional E is allowed, and S has no topological or cardinality restriction. Let V: E -> R be twice continuously Frechet differentiable, and let kappa be a real number with 1 <= kappa. Assume that for every x,v in E, kappa^(-1) ||v||^2 <= D(DV)(x)[v][v] <= ||v||^2, where D(DV)(x)[v][v] denotes the iterated actual real Frechet derivative. Let eta: S -> R and y: S -> E be measurable, and suppose eta(s) > 0 for every s in S. Define F(s,x) = V(x) + (eta(s)^(-1)/2) ||x - y(s)||^2. There exists a measurable p: S -> E such that all of the following hold simultaneously: (1) For every s, p(s) + eta(s) grad V(p(s)) = y(s), using real scalar multiplication and the real Hilbert Riesz gradient. (2) For every s in S and z in E, F(s,p(s)) + ((kappa^(-1) + eta(s)^(-1))/2) ||z - p(s)||^2 <= F(s,z), and [F(s,z) <= F(s,p(s)) if and only if z = p(s)]. (3) For every s,t in S, eta(s) = eta(t) implies ||p(s) - p(t)|| <= ||y(s) - y(t)||. With this same p, define G: S x E -> E by G(s,z) = grad V(p(s) + sqrt(eta(s)) z), using real scalar multiplication. Then G is measurable for the product measurable structure, and for every s,t in S and z,w in E, eta(s) = eta(t) implies ||G(s,z) - G(t,w)|| <= ||y(s) - y(t)|| + sqrt(eta(s)) ||z - w||. Furthermore, there exists a measurable probability kernel K from S to E such that, for every s, K(s) is the literal pushforward of the canonical centered covariance-identity Gaussian measure on E under z |-> G(s,z). For every s, the identity function u |-> u is Bochner integrable under K(s); and for every a in E and every real r, the function u |-> exp(r <a, u - m_s>), where m_s = integral_E v dK(s)(v) is the actual mean of this same output law, is Bochner integrable under K(s). The quantification includes a = 0 and all signs of r. No quantitative exponential-moment bound, equality of m_s to a separately specified gradient, sampling algorithm, or runtime guarantee is asserted.",
  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": "Real Hilbert geometry on finite-dimensional E; arbitrary measurable parameter space S; twice continuously differentiable potential V; real kappa; measurable eta and y; derived quadratic-regularized energy F; existential measurable p; derived gradient-output map G; existential probability kernel K; each output law actual Bochner mean m_s.",
    "domains": "E: Type with NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace R, CompleteSpace, FiniteDimensional R, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace, including dimension zero. S: Type with MeasurableSpace only. V: E -> R; kappa: R; eta: S -> R; y,p: S -> E; F: S -> E -> R; G: S x E -> E with product measurable structure; K: Kernel S E. x,v,z,w,a range over all E; s,t over all S; the exponential parameter over all R.",
    "quantifiers": "For every ambient E,S,V,kappa,eta,y and all displayed instances satisfying the premises, let F have the displayed body. There exists one p for which measurability, the proximal equation for every s, both energy assertions for every s,z, and equal-eta nonexpansiveness for every s,t all hold. Let G have the displayed body using that same p. Measurability of G and the equal-eta estimate for every s,t,z,w hold, and there exists K that is Markov, equals the displayed pushforward for every s, and for every s has an integrable identity function and an integrable centered exponential for every a and every signed real parameter.",
    "assumptions": "kappa >= 1; actual C^2 real Frechet differentiability of V; for every x,v, kappa^(-1)||v||^2 <= D(DV)(x)[v][v] <= ||v||^2; genuine measurability of eta and y; eta(s) > 0 pointwise. E is complete finite-dimensional real inner-product/Borel space; S is merely measurable. Neither p, F conclusions, G conclusions, K nor moment estimates are premise witnesses.",
    "conclusion": "There is measurable p obeying p(s)+eta(s) grad V(p(s))=y(s); quadratic energy growth with coefficient (kappa^(-1)+eta(s)^(-1))/2; and F(s,z)<=F(s,p(s)) iff z=p(s). For equal eta values, ||p(s)-p(t)||<=||y(s)-y(t)||. The resulting G(s,z)=grad V(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s)) z) is measurable and, when eta(s)=eta(t), its pair difference is bounded by ||y(s)-y(t)||+sqrt(eta(s))||z-w||. A Markov kernel K realizes the standard-Gaussian pushforward through G(s,.) and has finite first Bochner integrability and all-direction, all-signed centered exponential integrability.",
    "scopes_senses": "F(s,x)=V(x)+(eta(s)^(-1)/2)||x-y(s)||^2 is a let-defined energy. The energy inequality and minimum-characterizing equivalence are conjuncts within every s,z. Equal eta is an implication premise in both pair estimates, with no bound across unequal eta asserted. G is a let-defined map after p is chosen; K is existential within this same p/G scope. K(s) is the gradient-output law, and its centered exponential uses integral v dK(s)(v) from that exact law. The gradient is the real Hilbert Riesz representative of the actual Frechet derivative. Kernel measurability and Markov probability semantics are genuine, not hidden estimate data.",
    "constant_dependencies": "kappa is real and >=1; both Hessian bounds have exactly kappa^(-1) and 1. eta is measurable and strictly positive, with no global lower or upper bound. F uses eta(s)^(-1)/2; growth uses (kappa^(-1)+eta(s)^(-1))/2. The p estimate has constant 1 under equal eta; the G noise coefficient is sqrt(eta(s)) and its y coefficient is 1 under equal eta. The Gaussian is canonical centered covariance identity. No positive-dimension assumption, explicit dimension-dependent constant, exponential-moment upper bound, unbiasedness identity, algorithm or runtime claim occurs. All directions include zero; all real exponential parameters include zero and negatives."
  },
